Thank you.  I don't know that I will post the ascension, because it
feels kind of weak on the whole.  I've never had a luckier game than
this one (aside from a few things like the Amulet in the water).  I had
speed boots on level 1.  I got a WoW off a dead chap in the mines, so
armor was down to -13 pretty quick.  On level 43, I ran into another
dead chap (didn't know you could get bones files that deep, but hearse
is running on this machine I was playing on, so I guess there could be
a lot of oddities floating around out there.) who had not just
Firebrand, but a blessed +7 Firebrand (it didn't get cursed from
death).  So I used that the rest of the way up with a katana.

On the whole I used 14 wishes ;-).  A lot were for cockatrice corpses
for Wiz kills because that was getting truly annoying and problematic.
I lost my first life in the Valley of the Dead on the way up due to
multiple Double Trouble spells and too many monsters in the way.

I did have trouble with finding altars, the minetown one was cross
aligned, and the only other one that could be realigned didn't have to
be, but was down at level 15 or so in the regular dungeon.  The only
thing I got respectable from sacrificing was Snickersnee which I used
for 90% of the game.  I got crowned Hand of Elbereth while creating
holy water so that kind of put the kibosh on trying to get more without
a lot more luck.

But other than these little things, basically in this game, if I needed
something, I had it.  I even had 4  levels of Gehennom with the ladder
within 5-10 spaces of each other.  I had the AoLS when I needed it, and
I'd acquired another and so when I needed it in the Astral Plane I had
it there too.  It felt like I was greased up and running on rails at
high speed downhill.  I know there are ascensions where there is a LOT
more work involved (because I've been there too).

Anyhow, thanks for the help!

